                    209.0,
                    1369.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The OBQ method starts from the observation that Equation (1) can be written as the sum of the squared errors, over each row of W. Then, OBQ handles each row w independently, quantizing one weight at a time while always updating all not-yet-quantized weights, in order to compensate for the error incurred by quantizing a single weight. Since the corresponding objective is a quadratic,",
